---
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/siteUrl';
import StatusPill from '../../components/StatusPill.astro';
import FeatureVisual from '../../components/FeatureVisual.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Image Trace — Editable Vectors from Raster Artwork"
  description="Trace logos, line art, flat colour, pixel art, and silhouettes into editable Varve paths with an honest local-first preview."
>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <div class="feature-page">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href={sitePath('/features')}>Features</a> / Image trace
      </nav>

      <div class="feature-kicker"><StatusPill status="available" /></div>
      <h1>Trace the shape you need. Keep the editability you need.</h1>
      <p class="feature-intro">
        Turn a local raster asset into ordinary editable paths without sending the artwork away.
        Choose the tracing intent, prepare the source, inspect the result, and apply only when the
        preview is useful.
      </p>

      <FeatureVisual
        scene="vectorize"
        caption="The Vectorize workflow previews the prepared source, the trace overlay, and the actual fitted vector result before Apply."
      />

      <section class="workflow-band" aria-label="Image trace workflow">
        <div>
          <span class="workflow-label">01 · Intent</span>
          <strong>Choose a mode</strong>
          <span>Silhouette, line art, colour, pixel art, or desktop centerline.</span>
        </div>
        <span class="workflow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        <div>
          <span class="workflow-label">02 · Review</span>
          <strong>Prepare and compare</strong>
          <span>Use Source, Prepared, Overlay, Vector, anchors, and 1:1 inspection.</span>
        </div>
        <span class="workflow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        <div>
          <span class="workflow-label">03 · Edit</span>
          <strong>Apply ordinary paths</strong>
          <span>Keep the source, edit nodes, undo once, or re-trace from saved provenance.</span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section">
        <h2>Start with the artwork’s job</h2>
        <div class="mode-grid" aria-label="Tracing intents">
          <article class="mode-card mode-card--accent">
            <span class="mode-card__number">01</span>
            <h3>Logos and silhouettes</h3>
            <p>Filled contours, retained counters, useful corners, and compact curves for marks that need node editing.</p>
            <span class="mode-card__meta">Monochrome · cutout holes</span>
          </article>
          <article class="mode-card">
            <span class="mode-card__number">02</span>
            <h3>Scans and line art</h3>
            <p>Optional grayscale, denoise, fixed threshold, or adaptive threshold for uneven paper and light ink.</p>
            <span class="mode-card__meta">Reversible preparation</span>
          </article>
          <article class="mode-card">
            <span class="mode-card__number">03</span>
            <h3>Flat colour</h3>
            <p>Bounded palette quantization with separate fills. Use stacked output when independently simplified colour edges need cover.</p>
            <span class="mode-card__meta">Colour count · cutout or stacked</span>
          </article>
          <article class="mode-card">
            <span class="mode-card__number">04</span>
            <h3>Pixel art</h3>
            <p>Nearest-neighbour preparation and hard pixel-aligned regions, with no curve smoothing or anti-alias promise.</p>
            <span class="mode-card__meta">Exact within the declared budget</span>
          </article>
          <article class="mode-card">
            <span class="mode-card__number">05</span>
            <h3>Centerlines</h3>
            <p>Recover editable strokes with endpoints, branches, loops, and a measured stroke width instead of pretending an outline is a centerline.</p>
            <span class="mode-card__meta">Desktop native provider</span>
          </article>
          <article class="mode-card">
            <span class="mode-card__number">06</span>
            <h3>Photos and gradients</h3>
            <p>Use colour tracing as a bounded stylization. The result is an editable approximation, not recovered semantic objects or a reconstructed gradient.</p>
            <span class="mode-card__meta">Inspect complexity before Apply</span>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section">
        <h2>A preview you can trust</h2>
        <p>
          The preview is built from the same fitted curves, handles, holes, fills, and stroke
          semantics that are inserted into the document. It does not replace the committed artwork
          with a screenshot. Switch between the original source, prepared source, overlay, and
          vector result without tracing again; turn on anchors and use Fit or 1:1 when a narrow gap
          matters.
        </p>
        <p>
          Diagnostics expose path and anchor counts, holes, omitted regions, effective processing
          dimensions, provider, complexity, and downsampling. A draft preview is labelled when the
          final run can use a larger bounded raster.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section feature-section--note">
        <h2>Local-first, with honest boundaries</h2>
        <p>
          Ordinary tracing runs locally through the native desktop engine or bounded web fallbacks.
          It does not require an account, paid API, model download, GPU, or internet connection.
          Optional image models are not silently added to tracing, and the source asset is kept
          available for comparison and later editing.
        </p>
        <p>
          Tracing currently reads source pixels, not the selected image’s visible composited
          appearance. Masks, crops, adjustments, effects, and backdrop-dependent blending are
          called out in the workflow instead of being approximated silently. Shared-boundary
          cutout simplification, editable gradient recovery, and semantic text recognition are not
          promised. See the <a href={sitePath('/docs/tools/image-trace')}>image trace guide</a> for
          the complete capability boundary.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="feature-cta">
        <Button href={sitePath('/download')}>Download Varve</Button>
        <Button variant="secondary" href={sitePath('/docs/tools/image-trace')}>Read the image trace guide</Button>
        <Button variant="secondary" href={sitePath('/features/vector-tools')}>Explore vector tools</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .feature-page { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 0; }
  .breadcrumb { font-size: 0.875rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .breadcrumb a { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .feature-kicker { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .feature-page h1 { max-width: 780px; font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem); line-height: 1.02; font-family: var(--font-editorial); color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .feature-intro { max-width: 700px; font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .workflow-band { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 4rem; padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-card); background: var(--surface-muted); }
  .workflow-band div { display: grid; gap: 0.4rem; }
  .workflow-label, .mode-card__number { color: var(--text-tertiary); font: 0.75rem var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .workflow-band strong, .mode-card h3 { color: var(--text-primary); }
  .workflow-band span:last-child { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; }
  .workflow-arrow { color: var(--accent-primary); font-size: 1.4rem; }
  .feature-section { margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .feature-section h2 { color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
  .feature-section p { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; }
  .mode-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1rem; }
  .mode-card { min-height: 220px; padding: 1.25rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-card); background: var(--surface-card); }
  .mode-card--accent { border-color: var(--border-accent); background: var(--surface-accent-soft); }
  .mode-card h3 { margin: 2rem 0 0.65rem; font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .mode-card p { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; }
  .mode-card__meta { display: block; margin-top: 1.25rem; color: var(--text-tertiary); font-size: 0.8rem; }
  .feature-section--note { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-primary); padding-left: 1rem; }
  .feature-section a { color: var(--text-link); }
  .feature-cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-default); padding-top: 2rem; }
  .btn-secondary { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; padding: 0.7rem 1.1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-control); color: var(--text-primary); text-decoration: none; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .workflow-band { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .workflow-arrow { transform: rotate(90deg); justify-self: start; }
    .mode-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .mode-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .mode-card { min-height: auto; }
    .mode-card h3 { margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  }
</style>
